==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|last|ly}}.

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{context|sequence}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to mark the beginning of the last in a list of items or propositions.}}
#: ''Firstly, that's illegal; secondly, it has serious disadvantages; thirdly, it's not necessary; and '''lastly''', did I mention that it's illegal?''
# {{context|discourse marker}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to signal that the speaker is about to yield control of the conversation}}.

====Synonyms====
